      },
      "text": "p by relating it to Fourier coefficients of cusp forms with increasing level.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7519578622057547,
        "y0": 0.48642017865421794,
        "x1": 0.8821536793428308,
        "y1": 0.5015151283957742
      },
      "text": "This is possible",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764631084367341,
        "y0": 0.5039957990550031,
        "x1": 0.8823491514118669,
        "y1": 0.5190907487965594
      },
      "text": "as such valuations are Fourier coefficients of incoherent Eisenstein series with full level, and",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764631084367341,
        "y0": 0.5217233137650923,
        "x1": 0.8819582072737949,
        "y1": 0.5368182635066485
      },
      "text": "can be approximated by Fourier coefficients of coherent Eisenstein series with higher levels,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764631084367341,
        "y0": 0.5392989341658776,
        "x1": 0.5125488580441943,
        "y1": 0.5543938839074337
      },
      "text": "which are holomorphic Hilbert modular forms.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5243138331992954,
        "y0": 0.5392989341658776,
        "x1": 0.827057832206776,
        "y1": 0.5543938839074337
      },
      "text": "This is the content of Theorem 2.5.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8388223087086397,
        "y0": 0.5392989341658776,
        "x1": 0.8823518441393484,
        "y1": 0.5543938839074337
      },
      "text": "After",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764631084367341,
        "y0": 0.5568745545666627,
        "x1": 0.8819571102366728,
        "y1": 0.5719695043082189
      },
      "text": "this, we still need a bound of such Fourier coefficients in terms of the level. This is achieved",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764631084367341,
        "y0": 0.574450174967448,
        "x1": 0.8823522430619383,
        "y1": 0.5895451247090041
      },
      "text": "in Theorem 3.5 using Deligne’s bound and a bound of the Petersson norm of a cusp form",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764631084367341,
        "y0": 0.5920257953682331,
        "x1": 0.8823524425232333,
        "y1": 0.6071207451097893
      },
      "text": "in terms of its Fourier coefficients at the cusp ∞. Section 4 contains the proof of Theorem 1.1.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
